---
const ssrUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SSR_SITE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="Gridiron Atlas is an NFL dashboard with a separately deployed server-rendered experience."
		/>
		<title>Gridiron Atlas</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<p>GRIDIRON ATLAS</p>
			<h1>NFL coverage, from kickoff to final whistle.</h1>
			<p>
				The live dashboard runs as a separately deployed server-rendered service so schedules,
				scores, and player data stay current.
			</p>
			{ssrUrl ? (
				<a href={ssrUrl}>Open the live dashboard</a>
			) : (
				<p>The live dashboard URL will be published after its AWS deployment.</p>
			)}
		</main>
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	:global(*) {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	:global(body) {
		margin: 0;
		background: #09111f;
		color: #f8fafc;
		font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
	}

	main {
		display: grid;
		align-content: center;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		min-height: 100vh;
		max-width: 46rem;
		margin: auto;
		padding: 2rem;
	}

	p {
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	main > p:first-child {
		color: #fbbf24;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5rem);
		line-height: 1;
	}

	a {
		width: fit-content;
		padding: 0.8rem 1.1rem;
		border-radius: 0.4rem;
		background: #fbbf24;
		color: #09111f;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
</style>
